{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310659,"nonce":"9aYwgbOe9xE4Wa8rY/4m2msaMl0=","title":"Two cross-module access bugs found bringing up BERT (2026-07-14), both make a correctly-built nue object read as ZERO/garbage from another ...","message":"Surfaced bringing up `BertModel` (built in `nue.arch.BertArch`, methods run in `nue.arch`,\ninvoked from the `bert-embed` example). All four made a **correctly-constructed** object read\nas zero/garbage fields when accessed cross-module. Proven by tracing: `BertArch.build` read\n`m.meta.hiddenSize=384` right after `new`; the same object read `0` once accessed from Main.\n\n`loader.load()` returns `Module` (interface). `var m:BertModel = cast loader.load(path)` (one-arg\nunsafe cast) yields a reference whose field reads are all zero, even in the SAME module. The\ntwo-arg **checked** cast `cast(loader.load(path), BertModel)` recovers the layout and works.\nllama-chat already uses `cast(loaded.model, LlamaModel)` for exactly this reason.\n**Rule: never one-arg-`cast` an interface return to a concrete type; always `cast(x, T)`.**\n\nFields typed `Null\u003cEmbedding\u003e` / `Null\u003cLayerNorm\u003e` on BertModel read as corrupt pointers and\nSIGSEGV on access, while plain `Embedding` / `Array\u003cTransformerBlock\u003e` fields on the SAME object\n(even at a LATER field offset) read fine. So it's NOT positional offset drift — it's the\n`Null\u003cclass\u003e` wrapper specifically. Workaround: store optional pieces as a **non-null\nplaceholder** (reuse another real field) gated by a trailing `Bool` flag; apply only when the\nflag is set. (Distinct from [[bugs_null_primitive_field_gep_corruption]] which is Null\u003cPRIMITIVE\u003e\nafter a scalar field; this is Null\u003cCLASS\u003e.)\n\n`BertModel` originally lived in `nue` while `BertArch` (its constructor) lived in `nue.arch`.\nCross-package construction field-drifted (blocks.length read garbage). Moving BertModel to\n`nue.arch` (same package as the builder, mirroring `LlamaModel` next to `LlamaArch`) fixed the\nArray/struct field reads. LlamaModel works precisely because it is co-located with LlamaArch.\n\n`new(meta, ..., ?segmentEmbed, ?embedNorm, blocks, ?encoderNorm)` — optional params BEFORE\nrequired ones misbind fields cross-module. All-required + trailing Bool flags.\n\n**Root cause:** the known x-module SymbolId/layout-drift disease\n([[bugs_import_xmodule_member_resolution]], [[bugs_xmodule_resolution_disease_cluster]]). These\nare WORKAROUNDS; the general fix is declaration-first resolution. Any nue object accessed from an\nexample/server module must follow rules 1-4, OR expose a STATIC entry taking/returning primitives\n(what `nue.arch.BertEmbedder.goldenTest` does — all model access stays in-module).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_null_class_field_and_onearg_cast_xmodule` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}